=======================================================================
 test_poisson_3d - harness around test_Poisson_3D.lgi
=======================================================================

WHAT THIS IS

  Checks for the 3D Poisson disk sampler in LaGriT,

      createpts / poisson_disk / 3d_box / ...

  built around the existing deck test_Poisson_3D.lgi; its three .mlgi
  files are used UNCHANGED. The deck makes eight meshes of the box
  [0.2,0.8] x [0.2,0.8] x [0,0.3] (reduced from 1 x 1 x 0.3 on Oct 6
  2026 to cut run time; see THE BOX below): four with a uniform h,
  four with an h field that grows with distance from a vertical axis,
  with and without the edge buffer. Each is dumped as .inp and .stor.

  The harness runs the deck once and checks every output: properties
  any correct result must have are HARD checks; spacing, tet quality
  and .stor coefficients are MEASURED and reported so a change in the
  sampler shows up as a change in the numbers.

QUICK START

  ./run_test_poisson_3d.sh  [path-to-lagrit]       about 1 minute
                                  (LaGriT 44 s, checks ~25 s, picture 11 s)

  then open, in a web browser,

      logs/summary.html

  To re-check outputs already in this directory without running LaGriT:

  ./run_test_poisson_3d.sh --check-only

  Requires: LaGriT, Python 3 (standard library only), a POSIX shell.

