-----------------------------------------------------------------------
FINDINGS - all numbers below are from the ORIGINAL 1 x 1 x 0.3 box
(lagrit.out of Oct 1 2026 and case 05; full harness run of Oct 6 2026)
-----------------------------------------------------------------------

  1. The Oct 1 lagrit.out had every driver message cut at its first
     blank and right-justified (Begin banner "===", exit line
     "poisson_disk_3d"). That was an older build: the Oct 6 run's
     lagrit.out has all 8 full "poisson_disk_3d exit" lines. The
     harness splits the log on the echoed createpts command and
     accepts either form of exit line.

  2. Face lattice spacing is not h. The driver builds the face brick
     with n = ceiling(L/h) POINTS per axis, so spacing L/(n-1): 1.026 h
     along x and y and 1.091 h along z at h = 0.025. Confirmed by the
     brick sizes in lagrit.out (40x40x12, 80x80x24, 125x125x38).

  3. The face lattice ignores the h field. It always uses H_REFINE_SIZE
     (the field's floor). In case 08 that puts 49 106 of the 67 958
     nodes (72 %) on the faces, spaced 0.008 where the field asks for
     up to 0.07.

  4. Buffer 0.5 h (case 03) gives 1646 wrong-sign coefficients, more
     than no buffer at all (case 01, 371). Buffers of 1 h and 2 h give
     none. Case 03 is therefore "reported", not judged.

  5. Without a buffer (case 05) the sampler itself puts 1545 nodes on
     the faces, corners included, and the mesh fills the box exactly.
     Face-face pairs come as close as 0.67 h (94 pairs under 0.9 h);
     interior pairs as close as 0.82 h. Slivers: smallest dihedral
     0.35 deg, 80 tets under 5 deg.

  6. Oct 6 harness run: every HARD check passes on all eight cases,
     including the buffered ones (mesh boundary = the box, no
     zero-volume tets). Wrong-sign .stor pairs: 01 371, 03 1646,
     05 180, all others 0.

  7. Interior pairs closer than h in EVERY case: smallest
     d / max(h_p, h_q) between interior nodes is 0.63 - 0.82
     (01 0.816, 02 0.687, 04 0.655, 08 0.631). The 2D sampler's
     uniform case was 0.991. Slivers in every case; smallest dihedral
     0.049 deg (case 08). Reported, not judged.

  8. The field row SKIPs: the dump line in test_user_resolution.mlgi
     is commented out. The field varies in x and y only, so these
     cases do not exercise the bug-5 fix (all z layers checked) with
     a z-varying field.

-----------------------------------------------------------------------
WHAT TO EDIT WHEN SOMETHING CHANGES
-----------------------------------------------------------------------

  Deck defines changed     edit the matching case line in
                           test_Poisson_3D.cases; the deck row FAILS
                           until they agree
  Case added to the deck   add a case line, in deck order
  h field formula changed  make_field() in check_test_poisson_3d.py
  Want the field checked   uncomment the dump line in
                           test_user_resolution.mlgi; only the last
                           radial run's dump survives (case 08)
  A wrong-sign expectation stor_neg=0 or stor_neg=report per case
